{
  "name": "sky_falloff_rebuild_cost",
  "description": "What ONE whole-map \u00a77c BFS rebuild costs. falloff_rebuild_ms is the number to read: it forces ten rebuilds with a stopwatch around each and reports the mean, because Rebuild runs once per map per invalidation (lazily, on the next read) and so appears in no Dubs per-frame window, while the Circinus arms kept here alongside it proved unreliable -- 24 calls / 442.67 ms on one run and 0 calls on the next for the SAME build, with circinus_falloff_patched reading 1 and the depth probes returning 2 in both. The PlaceThings/Probe pairs dirty and re-read the grid by hand so the Circinus arms have something to count at all. Compare the same probe across two builds, never two arms in one run. Pins circinus_available at 1 so a run without Circinus (astryl.Circinus, 3773680130) fails loudly rather than reporting a confident zero. The falloff_* checksum probes at the end are the oracle for any rewrite of the BFS: they hash every cell's depth and strength, so bit-identity is measured over the whole map rather than over the handful of cells the other scenarios pin. Capture them on the OLD build before changing it.",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "requiredMods": {
    "astryl.Circinus": "3773680130"
  },
